 "intro_html": "A Korean cookbook recipe: the cabbage is brined, salted for 12 hours under a weight, rinsed, then filled leaf by leaf <b>from the middle out</b> with a gochugaru filling and wrapped in its own outer leaves. <b>Your additions</b> go into the filling: dried baby anchovies and sakura shrimp chopped with a knife, and pear juice squeezed through cheesecloth.",
