 "notes": [
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Based on the recipe in <i>Easy Korean Cooking</i> (cookbook), with your additions: dried baby anchovies, sakura shrimp and pear juice.</li><li>The amounts of your additions are a starting guess — adjust them next batch.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Source"
  },
  {
   "html": "<p>If you can’t get salted anchovy or salted shrimp sauce, fish sauce stands in for either — but the Korean versions are worth hunting down.</p>",
   "title_html": "Fish sauce instead of the Korean sauces"
  },
  {
   "html": "<p>Use coarse salt for both the brine and the leaves — fine table salt is saltier by volume and lands unevenly.</p>",
   "title_html": "Coarse salt"
  },
  {
   "html": "<p>Kombu stock — see <a href=\"shiitake-kombu-dashi.html\">shiitake-kombu dashi</a>.</p>",
   "title_html": "Kelp stock"
  },
  {
   "html": "<p>See also <a href=\"kkakdugi.html\">kkakdugi</a>.</p>",
   "title_html": "Radish kimchi"
  }
 ],
