 "sources": [],
 "steps": [
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Stir <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"cup\" data-a=\"1\" data-s=\"0\">1 cup</span> of <b>coarse salt</b> into <b><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"l\" data-a=\"2\" data-s=\"0\">2 l</span> of water</b> in a bowl big enough to hold half a cabbage.</li><li>Peel off the outer leaves and <b>keep them</b> — they wrap the kimchi in step 6.</li><li>Cut the cabbage in half lengthwise and dunk the halves in the brine.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-1",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Brine and halve",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Peel off the outer leaves and keep them — they wrap the kimchi at the end.",
      "src": "illustrations/kimchi/1-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Cut the cabbage in half lengthwise.",
      "src": "illustrations/kimchi/1-how2.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Dunk the halves in the brine.",
      "src": "illustrations/kimchi/1-how3.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/kimchi/1.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 1,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~15 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~15 min</span>",
   "title": "Brine and halve",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"count\" data-a=\"1\" data-f=\"head|heads\" data-n=\"1\">1 head</span> (~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"kg\" data-a=\"2.5\">2.5 kg</span>)",
     "name_html": "Napa cabbage"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"cup\" data-a=\"1\">1 cup</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"200\" data-alt=\"1\">200 ml</span>)</span>",
     "name_html": "Coarse salt, for the brine"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"l\" data-a=\"2\">2 l</span>",
     "name_html": "Water"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Take the halves out and work the second cup of <b>coarse salt</b> in between the leaves, mostly onto the thick white stems.</li><li>Leave them <b>cut faces up</b> for <b>7 hours</b> (12 in winter), then flip them <b>face down</b> for <b>5 hours</b> more.</li><li>Keep weight on them throughout — a heavy plate or board, or a bag of water — so the salt gets in evenly.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-2",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Salt and press",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Lift the leaves and sprinkle coarse salt between them, mostly on the thick white stems.",
      "src": "illustrations/kimchi/2-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Press them under a heavy plate — 7 hours cut-side up, then 5 hours cut-side down.",
      "src": "illustrations/kimchi/2-how2.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/kimchi/2.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 2,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "12 h (17 h in winter)",
   "time_html": "<span>12 h (17 h in winter)</span>",
   "title": "Salt and press",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"cup\" data-a=\"1\">1 cup</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"200\" data-alt=\"1\">200 ml</span>)</span>",
     "name_html": "Coarse salt, between the leaves"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Wash the salt off under cold water, opening the leaves so it reaches inside.</li><li>Stand the halves in a colander and let them drip for about <b>an hour</b>.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-3",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Rinse and drain",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Rinse thoroughly in cold water, opening the leaves.",
      "src": "illustrations/kimchi/3-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/kimchi/3.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 3,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~1 h",
   "time_html": "<span>~1 h</span>",
   "title": "Rinse and drain",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Slice the <b>daikon</b> into thin <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"0.3\" data-s=\"0\">0.3 cm</span> matchsticks; cut the <b>green onions</b> into <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"3\" data-s=\"0\">3 cm</span> pieces.</li><li>Your additions — chop finely with a knife:<ul class=\"ing\"><li>dried baby anchovies <span class=\"amt\">a small handful (~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"10\">10 g</span>) — enough to taste a little</span></li><li>dried sakura shrimp <span class=\"amt\">a small handful (~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"5\" data-b=\"10\">5–10 g</span>) — the same idea</span></li></ul></li><li>Crush or grate the <b>garlic</b> — a ceramic grater is best, a fine metal one works too.</li><li>Grate the ginger and squeeze it through cheesecloth for the <b>ginger juice</b>.</li><li>Grate the <b>Asian pear</b>, put it in cheesecloth and squeeze out the juice — the juice is what you want.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-4",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Prepare the filling",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Daikon: slice into thin 3 mm planks.",
      "src": "illustrations/kimchi/4-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Stack a few planks and cut them into 0.3 cm matchsticks.",
      "src": "illustrations/kimchi/4-how2.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Green onions: line them up and cut into 3 cm lengths.",
      "src": "illustrations/kimchi/4-how3.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Your additions: chop the dried anchovies and shrimp finely with a knife.",
      "src": "illustrations/kimchi/4-how4.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Grate the garlic and ginger on a ceramic grater, rubbing in small circles.",
      "src": "illustrations/kimchi/4-how5.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Squeeze the grated pear (and ginger) through cheesecloth — the juice is what you want.",
      "src": "illustrations/kimchi/4-how6.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/kimchi/4.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 4,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~25 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~25 min</span>",
   "title": "Prepare the filling",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"200\">200 g</span>",
     "name_html": "Daikon"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"50\">50 g</span>",
     "name_html": "Green onions"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"2\">2 tbsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Garlic"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tbsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Ginger juice"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"count\" data-a=\"0.5\" data-n=\"1\">½</span> (~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"150\">150 g</span>)",
     "name_html": "Asian pear"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Gloves on. Mix everything from step 4 with:<ul class=\"ing two-col\"><li>gochugaru (Korean chilli powder) <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"cup\" data-a=\"1\">1 cup</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"200\" data-alt=\"1\">200 ml</span>)</span></span></li><li>salted anchovy sauce <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"100\">100 ml</span></span></li><li>salted shrimp sauce <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"3\">3 tbsp</span></span></li><li>sugar <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"4\">4 tbsp</span></span></li><li>kelp (kombu) stock <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"100\">100 ml</span></span></li></ul></li><li>Let it stand about <b>30 minutes</b> so the flavours come together.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-5",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Mix the filling",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Gloves on: mix the gochugaru, sauces, sugar and stock with everything from step 4.",
      "src": "illustrations/kimchi/5-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/kimchi/5.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 5,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~5 min + 30 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~5 min + 30 min</span>",
   "title": "Mix the filling",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li><b>Start at the middle:</b> lift the innermost leaf next to the core and smear filling over it right down to the core.</li><li>Lay it back, lift the next leaf out from the middle and repeat — work <b>outward</b> until every leaf is coated.</li><li>Fold the outer leaves you saved around each half like a parcel, so none of the filling escapes.</li><li>Press the parcels into an airtight jar and give them <b>5–7 days</b> in the fridge before eating.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-6",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Fill, wrap and pack",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Start at the middle: lift the innermost leaf and smear filling down to the core.",
      "src": "illustrations/kimchi/6-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Lay it back, lift the next leaf out from the middle, repeat.",
      "src": "illustrations/kimchi/6-how2.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Work outward until the outer leaves are done.",
      "src": "illustrations/kimchi/6-how3.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Wrap each half in the outer leaves you kept.",
      "src": "illustrations/kimchi/6-how4.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Pack tightly into an airtight jar, then 5–7 days in the fridge.",
      "src": "illustrations/kimchi/6-how5.webp"
     }
    ],
